# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
#  Weights, runtimes and vendored binaries. The checkout is 45 GB and GitHub's hard
#  per-file limit is 100 MB, so none of this can go up: the three Anima checkpoints are
#  4-5.6 GB each, the 9B GGUF is 5.4 GB, the embedded Python and the kohya venv are
#  thousands of files. These are downloaded by the setup scripts, not committed.
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
models/
trainer/
tools/gguf/
tools/llamacpp/
tools/llamacpp-cpu/
tools/MinGit/
ComfyUI_windows_portable/
_dl/
env/
agent/
.workbuddy/

# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
#  Runtime state and generated output.
#
#  workspace/refs/ is third-party doujin artwork collected from the web - committing it
#  would redistribute someone else's copyrighted work. workspace/out/ is adult imagery
#  this pipeline generated, and GitHub's terms do not permit sexual content in
#  repositories. Neither belongs here, and neither is needed to run the code: the refs
#  are inputs you supply yourself and the output is regenerated by running the pipeline.
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
workspace/refs/
workspace/out/
workspace/logs/
workspace/jobs/
workspace/

# Generated renders and test captures anywhere in the tree.
*.png
*.jpg
*.jpeg
*.webp
*.gif
*.mp4

# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
#  Downloaded llama.cpp CUDA builds. These are release zips (~562 MB together, one of
#  them 413 MB on its own, over the 100 MB hard limit). They are fetched by the setup
#  scripts and are someone else's redistributable, not our source.
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
_stage/llamacpp_cuda/

# Collected samples of other artists' work, gathered to study a style. Same reasoning as
# workspace/refs/ above - committing them redistributes artwork we do not own.
_stage/artist_samples/

# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
#  Third-party ComfyUI node packs, vendored into _stage/ for local experiments.
#  Neither ships a LICENSE file, and "no license" means all rights reserved - they are
#  not ours to redistribute. Install them from their own upstream repositories instead;
#  see "外部依赖" in README.txt for where each one comes from.
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
_stage/promptkit/
_stage/anima_incontext/

# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
#  Generated preset library. build_presets.py scrapes booru tag data and writes this
#  file; it carries a `generated` timestamp and a `sources` block, so it is a build
#  artifact rather than source. Regenerate it locally with build_presets.py. Shipping
#  it would also mean redistributing a scraped tag/artist corpus, which is not ours.
#  artist_styles.json is hand-curated and stays tracked.
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
pipeline/presets/presets.json

# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
#  Python / editor noise
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*.egg-info/
.venv/
venv/
.vscode/
.idea/
Thumbs.db
desktop.ini
*.log
pipeline/presets/restricted_tags.txt

# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
#  Internal research note. MODEL_SELECTION_2026.md is a model survey written around a
#  specific content brief, and rewriting it neutrally would destroy its value as a
#  record of what was actually evaluated. It stays local; the technical conclusions are
#  already reflected in README.md and the code comments.
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
_stage/MODEL_SELECTION_2026.md
